Patch 2050: a vertex range already copied into the vertex-pulling ring in this batch is reused, not copied again
(VPULL_REUSE=0 off). Diagnostic VPULL_DUP=1 adds the bytes that repeat an earlier copy ('dup') to the [VPULL] line.

With pulling on for 99% of draws (2049) the drawing thread copied about 2.5 GB/s of guest vertex bytes into the ring,
about 126 MB per demo fight frame; a quarter repeated an earlier copy exactly, and several-stream draws share streams.
A new single-stream record whose range was copied before sits on that copy (and is not extended); several-stream
records address their streams from the ring start, each reused or copied once. A table of (guest offset, length,
memory) -> ring offset is emptied whenever the ring restarts.

Tested (US disc, bench.ps1): ring copies 12.6 -> 7.0 GB per 5 s, drain per demo frame 24.6 -> 22.9 ms; demo
20.68 / 20.52 / 21.00 flips/s (median 20.68, before 20.51), Free Battle 20.00 (before 19.84); pictures right
(bench\exp\2026-11-07_1727-vpullreuse2).

